From 043b7e0a962d05e862e72e59cad32aa3fa2df7b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:50:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(ui): drag rings in Rotate mode turn the selected
 part

The viewport bar gets a Rotate button next to Move. With Rotate on, the
one selected part shows three rings round its bounding-box centre, one
square to each shown axis, at a constant 60 px on screen. A drag on a
ring turns the part about that axis through the centre as a preview,
with the signed angle above the bar. The release queues one
TurnModelBy, which runs the existing MoveModel: one undo step, the
generated paths go stale, the stock follows. Escape cancels; a turn
that ends at its start adds no step and no rotation noise.

Fixes #2047

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
